CONTROLLER FIXES - UE4SS NOT REQUIRED
Build Instructions
Release: v1.3.4

The native DLL was built with LLVM/Clang 17 and LLD 17 for 64-bit Windows.

Files used:
- source\controller_lock.cpp
- source\kernel32.def
- source\user32.def
- source\version_compat.def

From the source folder:

1. Create the Windows import libraries:

lld-link /lib /def:kernel32.def /machine:x64 /out:kernel32.lib

lld-link /lib /def:user32.def /machine:x64 /out:user32.lib


2. Compile the source:

clang++ -target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc -c controller_lock.cpp -o controller_lock.obj -O2 -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti -fno-stack-protector -fno-unwind-tables -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables


3. Link the DLL:

lld-link /dll /entry:DllMain /nodefaultlib /subsystem:windows /machine:x64 controller_lock.obj kernel32.lib user32.lib /def:version_compat.def /timestamp:1788489263 /out:DawnwalkerControllerFix.dll


Verification
============
The expected SHA-256 for the release DLL is:

95FE31CB82D60B68A8D4D4FE7EDA22CF848667C733CBC202C16724C34F396CA7

PowerShell can be used to check it:

(Get-FileHash .\DawnwalkerControllerFix.dll -Algorithm SHA256).Hash

The fixed /timestamp value is included because the PE header timestamp affects
the final file hash. Using the commands above reproduces the submitted release
DLL byte-for-byte.


Installer
=========
The installer source is included as:

- source\SETUP.bat
- source\Setup.ps1

The installer locates Dawnwalker.exe, copies/backups/restores the DLL files,
calculates SHA-256 hashes, and edits Dawnwalker's local Engine.ini.

It adds:

[ConsoleVariables]
Slate.EnableSyntheticCursorMoves=0

The release payload is named DawnwalkerControllerFix.dll in the download.
During installation it is copied beside Dawnwalker.exe as version.dll.
Standard version.dll exports are forwarded through version_chain.dll.

